{"id": 13, "ts": 1781181792.8716109, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s clear articulation of Candidate\u202fC\u2019s reliability, rapid correct decision\u2011making, and crew\u2011positive attitude. Those are indeed core to our long\u2011distance pilot role. However, before we settle, I want to highlight that Candidate\u202fD also demonstrates strong reliability \u2013 he \u201ctakes responsibility seriously\u201d and \u201cresponds to unexpected events adequately,\u201d which speaks to both operational consistency and stress handling. Yet, his professional communication is flagged as a \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d attitude with a \u201chot temper,\u201d raising concerns about crew cooperation and professionalism in the cockpit.\nConversely, we still lack any concrete observations on Candidate\u202fA\u2019s stress resilience or operational reliability, which are essential for assessing his suitability. Without that data, it\u2019s difficult to weigh his strong technical vision and leadership against the unknowns.\nGiven the current evidence, Candidate\u202fC still appears the most balanced choice, but we should continue probing Candidate\u202fA\u2019s reliability and Candidate\u202fB\u2019s decision quality before finalizing."}
